	url = {https://osf.io/preprints/edarxiv/9r3ps_v1/},
	abstract = {There has been a robust body of work in the Constructionist paradigm on the value of having students
program for math and science learning. In this opinion piece, we build from the premise that students
programming for math and science learning continues to remain relevant in an era in which AI systems can
rapidly generate code. Drawing on key tenets in Constructionism from decades of work, we propose what we
see as productive directions for future work in order to make student programming in the age of AI systems
